==Trivia==
* Nebel was used as the [[Original Trainer|OT]] of {{p|Volcanion}} event distribution for {{g|X and Y}} and {{pkmn|Omega Ruby and Alpha Sapphire}}, a reference to the nineteenth movie {{OBP|Volcanion|M19}} in Nebel Plateau.
* The Nebel Plateau resembles the later-introduced [[Cero Island]] in being home to Pokémon who live in remote, forested highlands, had been harmed by humans, fear humans, and are protected by a powerful Pokémon: [[Volcanion (M19)]] or [[Mewtwo (M01)]].

===Origin===
{{main|Pokémon world in relation to the real world#In the movies|Pokémon world in relation to the real world → In the movies}}
Nebel Plateau is modeled after various locations in {{wp|Hokkaido}}, Japan<ref>[https://twitter.com/dora6669/status/1674559383244783617 Tweet by Shinji Miyazaki (@dora6669). Tweeted June 30, 2023.] (Japanese and English)</ref><ref>[https://twitter.com/dora6669/status/1548166277352812544 Tweet by Shinji Miyazaki (@dora6669). Tweeted July 16, 2022.] (Japanese)</ref><ref>[https://twitter.com/dora6669/status/1548166609432645632 Tweet by Shinji Miyazaki (@dora6669). Tweeted July 16, 2022.]</ref><ref>[https://twitter.com/dora6669/status/1614470355409850372 Tweet by Shinji Miyazaki (@dora6669). Tweeted July 16, 2022.] (Japanese)</ref>, where the production team had {{wp|Location scouting|scouted}} {{wp|Lake Mashū}}, {{wp|Lake Tōya}} and Osaru River in {{wp|Shikotsu-Tōya National Park}}, Kaiyōdai Observatory in {{wp|Nakashibetsu, Hokkaido|Nakashibetsu}}, along with {{wp|Mount Iō (Shiretoko)|Mount Iō}}, Oshinkoshin Falls, and {{wp|Shiretoko National Park}} in the {{wp|Shiretoko Peninsula}}.

